{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 7, :comments ["And the reason for <b>if he has not put forth his hand against his neighbor's property</b>: according to Rashi's opinion, he is to draw near to the Elohim to swear that he did not put forth his hand against his fellow's property. But the correct interpretation is that he is to draw near to the Elohim to swear that it was stolen, just as he claims — that he did not put forth his hand to use it for his own needs against his neighbor's property, for one who puts forth his hand against a deposit becomes liable as a robber and is liable for unavoidable loss."], :book :exodus, :voice :ramban, :lang :en, :chapter 22, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T03:13:54.567625718Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}